  "historical_output_text": " I used this trail to get somewhere, or somewhere back when the leaves fell off and covered up everything, hiding what lay underneath until I could no see anymore and I had lost myself in my day and my daydream and the only things left to walk on where the dead trees, and it didn‘t even really make sense that you were still alive in that kind or darkness.\n\nI was always so used, so comfortable in these walks through my neighborhood trail but now I could only remember what had always been there but the trail had always just seemed a constant. The path, that had led so easily from where we lived to where you would have gone if only you could see it.\n\nI took another breath and I could taste the autumn. There was still so many things in life you can only smell, feel or only taste if they're right before it",
